========================================================================================
TAKEAWAY
========================================================================================
  1. The exact phase-color reservoir admits a deterministic lower bound:
        actual_count(q=14V) >= V*Sigma(P,E) - K(P,E).
  2. This proves every fixed (P,E) shape for all V > K/Sigma, reducing
     the finite placement problem to a computable small-V check.
  3. The remaining proof burden is now sharper: prove a uniform Sigma
     floor and a relation-lattice/tail bound showing K/Sigma is below
     the available V scale, or enumerate the finite residue tail.
  4. LRC(14) is still not proved; the obstruction has been compressed
     from colored CRT placement to a boundary-complexity inequality.
